- At the first bus stop, 5 more people got in, so the total became \( x + 5 \).
- At the second bus stop, 7 people got down and 8 more got in. The net change is \( -7 + 8 = +1 \), so the total became \( (x + 5) + 1 = x + 6 \).

After the second stop, there were 20 people heading to the third stop, so:
\[
x + 6 = 20
\]

Solving for \( x \):
\[
x = 20 - 6 = 14
\]

Thus, 14 people got on the bus at the terminal.

