With four turtles, their combined speed is \( 4 \times \frac{\text{distance}}{108} = \frac{4\text{distance}}{108} = \frac{\text{distance}}{27} \) per hour.

The time to cover the distance is the reciprocal of the combined speed: \( \frac{\text{distance}}{\frac{\text{distance}}{27}} = 27 \) hours.

Alternatively, the four turtles are equivalent to two kangaroos in speed (since \( 4 \times \frac{1}{2} = 2 \)), and two kangaroos take the same time as three kangaroos, which is 18 hours.

Thus, it will take 27 hours for the four turtles to cross the highway.

