The combined age of all three is 100 years. So, Peter + Paul + Jean = 100.

Substituting the expressions:

(2J + 10) + (J + 10) + J = 100

Now, combine like terms: 2J + J + J is 4J, and 10 + 10 is 20. So, 4J + 20 = 100.

Subtract 20 from both sides: 4J = 80.

Then, divide by 4: J = 20.

So, John is 20 years old.

