Janet needs to save 20% of the $10,000 car downpayment, which is \(0.20 \times 10000 = 2000\) dollars.

Her total hourly earnings are $10 from wages plus $15 from tips, totaling $25 per hour.

She works 40 hours per week, so her weekly earnings are \(40 \times 25 = 1000\) dollars.

To save $2000, she needs \(2000 \div 1000 = 2\) weeks.

